; DisplaySyncCheck -- the launcher's display options reach the game
; (docs/concept-display-sync.md): -Y now (copied at once: RadeonGLFlip copy,
; sync off) with -X on (smooth scrolling: on FS-UAE's null card the blank
; clock is not there, so it switches itself off), then -Y blank -X off
; (copied, sync on). GL, orig01, 20 s each. FS-UAE + RadeonGL's null card.
; LIMIT 600
FailAt 1000
Wait 5
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/zod-#?
SetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax 16
Echo "=== GL, -Y now -X on ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZod dsn 20 -Y now -X on -m Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-dsn.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-dsn.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== GL, -Y blank -X off ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunZod dsb 20 -Y blank -X off -m Data/Campaing/Z_original/p02_bb_orig01.map
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/zod-dsb.done
Type DEV:Test/zod-dsb.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
UnSetEnv RadeonGLHeapMax
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
